<title>PORTUGAL: Portucel sees loss for 1996, Q4 pulp price unch.</title>
<headline>Portucel sees loss for 1996, Q4 pulp price unch.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese pulp group Portucel Industrial expects to post a loss in 1996 as profits in the fourth quarter would not be enough to cover losses early in the year, company president Jorge Godinho said.</p>
<p>He told Reuters pulp prices would stay unchanged at 420 Ecus per tonne in the fourth quarter this year.</p>
<p>&quot;I expect positive results in the last quarter, but they will not be enough to cover the negative impact in the first part of the year,&quot; Godinho said.  </p>
<p>Portucel shares dropped 30 escudos to 920 in volume of 197,125 shares at 1620 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
